   "text": {
    "L1": "Parity means checking whether a number is odd or even, without needing its exact value.",
    "L2": "An even number splits into pairs. An odd number has pairs and one left over.",
    "L3": "When two odd numbers meet, their two leftovers make one more pair.",
    "L4": "So odd plus odd is even, while odd plus even is odd.",
    "L5": "Here is the worked example: seven odd numbers cannot add to 100.",
    "L6": "Pair six of them to get an even total. The seventh is odd, so the whole sum is odd.",
    "L7": "Therefore 100 cannot be the sum of seven odd numbers. Parity proves it without trying every choice.",
    "L8": "Now decide whether five odd numbers can add up to 50."
   },
